Arnold shaders shouldn't overwrite a foreign shader prim in a bound material

A material authored by another exporter (here a MaterialX network like the one
mayaUSD writes) already holds shader prims named like the arnold ones. Writing
the arnold scene on top of it, in append mode over two frames, must leave these
prims untouched and author the arnold shading tree in an "arnold" node graph
under the material, connected to the material through node graph outputs. This
also applies when only a texture collides (a UsdPreviewSurface material sharing
a file texture with an arnold shader of another name). A material created by
the writer itself keeps its shaders directly under it. The file is read back to
check the arnold shaders are found through the node graph.

See #2803

author: sebastien.ortega
